    "body": "Took a look at the WS errors first since there were a ton of them. They're all 502s from nginx for `/websockets`. I checked the host and the wssServer node process was just not running.\n\nChecking in the journalctl i saw this\n```php\nrun.sh[8437]: node:internal/webstreams/readablestream:1077\nrun.sh[8437]:       throw new ERR_INVALID_STATE.TypeError('Controller is already closed');\nrun.sh[8437]:             ^\nrun.sh[8437]: TypeError [ERR_INVALID_STATE]: Invalid state: Controller is already closed\nrun.sh[8437]:     at ReadableStreamDefaultController.enqueue (node:internal/webstreams/readablestream:1077:13)\nrun.sh[8437]:     at Object.next (/opt/homarr/apps/websocket/wssServer.cjs:775:22)\nrun.sh[8437]:     at Object.next (/opt/homarr/apps/websocket/wssServer.cjs:706:100)\nrun.sh[8437]:     at /opt/homarr/apps/websocket/wssServer.cjs:854233:20\nrun.sh[8437]:     at /opt/homarr/apps/websocket/wssServer.cjs:224095:17\nrun.sh[8437]:     at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:103:5) {\nrun.sh[8437]:   code: 'ERR_INVALID_STATE'\nrun.sh[8437]: }\nrun.sh[8437]: Node.js v24.13.0\n```\n\nBasically once the WS server dies every page fails. wssServer.cjs is huge so I'll keep digging for a while.\n\nEdit: \n\nsome findings\n\ngrep around the problem line to find some context and we see some function named observableToReadableStream\n```ts\n# sed -n '760,790p' /opt/homarr/apps/websocket/wssServer.cjs\n    });\n  });\n  return promise2;\n}\nfunction observableToReadableStream(observable$1, signal3) {\n  let unsub = null;\n  const onAbort = () => {\n    unsub === null || unsub === void 0 || unsub.unsubscribe();\n    unsub = null;\n    signal3.removeEventListener(\"abort\", onAbort);\n  };\n  return new ReadableStream({\n    start(controller) {\n      unsub = observable$1.subscribe({\n        next(data) {\n          try { controller.enqueue({\n            ok: true,\n            value: data\n          }); } catch (_e) { /* stream closed */ }\n        },\n        error(error52) {\n          try { controller.enqueue({\n            ok: false,\n            error: error52\n          }); } catch (_e) {}\n          try { controller.close(); } catch (_e) {}\n        },\n        complete() {\n          try { controller.close(); } catch (_e) {}\n        }\n      });\n```\n**be aware that this file is modified locally!! the real deal doesn't have the try catches. Im getting to that.**\n\nAnd grepping `observableToReadableStream` returns \n\n```bash\nroot@HomarrDEV:~ # grep -rnHo 'observableToReadableStream' /root/homarr/node_modules/\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/dist/observable-B1Nk6r1H.cjs:91:observableToReadableStream\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/dist/observable-B1Nk6r1H.cjs:128:observableToReadableStream\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/dist/observable-UMO3vUa_.mjs:90:observableToReadableStream\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/dist/observable-UMO3vUa_.mjs:127:observableToReadableStream\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/dist/observable-UMO3vUa_.mjs.map:1:observableToReadableStream\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/dist/observable-UMO3vUa_.mjs.map:1:observableToReadableStream\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/src/observable/observable.ts:128:observableToReadableStream\n/root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc/server/src/observable/observable.ts:172:observableToReadableStream\n```\n\nThe only files that makes sense is `observable.ts`\n\nI believe this file is generated from `websocket/src/main.ts`. And honestly idk where to go from there. I started grepping the imports  (`grep -rnHo 'ReadableStream' /root/homarr/node_modules/@trpc`) to see if anything rings a bell and found something from trpc that rings a bell: [@trpc/server/src/observable/observable.ts](https://github.com/trpc/trpc/blob/main/packages/server/src/observable/observable.ts)\n\nAnd... well since this is an upstream lib I went back to the cjs file, I wrapped every controller call with a trycatch like the snippet above and the ws errors went away. **Looks like trpc is not checking if the controller even exists and dies.**\n\nMaybe we should open a bug report to trpc or control that error in homarr, but i wouldn't know where and I still want to find out what the other 2 errors are lol.\n\n\n\n\n",
